  "plain": "In the 1980s the UFO researcher Bill Moore published a report on the MJ-12 papers, documents describing a secret group said to handle crashed saucers. Among them is one dated 18 November 1952 that presents itself as a briefing for Eisenhower. Moore's report appeared in a book called The MJ12 Papers, and according to the writer Greg Bishop, who relays what he knows of Moore's work, it judged the documents \"compelling but not conclusive.\" Bishop tells Michels this to show that even the papers' first promoter stopped short of calling them genuine."
